A||N||4||Discover||Power Door Locks will not stop locking...Please help||||1||
Z||000000||Discover||11-20-2001||10:53 PM||||I have a 1988 GT and the Power Door Locks will not stop locking.  Both the right and left door lock solenoids pulse alternately about every 10 seconds until the battery runs down. Today I discovered that with one door open the locking stops. With either door open when I push in the door jamb switch it causes the door locks to lock.<P>Any body have a clue as to how to fix??<P>Thanks,<BR>Ned||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||11-21-2001||02:02 AM||||Don't have a fix for you at the moment, but for the time being, pull the plug on your door lock relay!<P>Look under the dash - right hand side - just above the kick panel on the r/h outter wall - look up and forward - big silver unit with a big plug on it.  Pull that off, and at least your battery won't drop dead.<P>While you're there, make sure the ground cable that's just below and to the right of the relay is intact and solidly attached (and not corroded, etc).<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-21-2001||05:30 AM||||try swapping the relay with somebody elses to see if that the prob. If still does it, id say you have bad ground somewhere or wiring short. Maybe short in lock motor itself.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-21-2001||08:01 AM||||Any kind of liquid in the door push button can short the contacts inside the door lock switch.  These may need to be removed, cleaned and dried carefully, then reinstalled.  Or maybe one even needs to be replaced.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Bluemagic||11-21-2001||08:33 AM||||This vehicle has a door lock module located in the driver kick panel that supply a positive pulse  to operate the locks however they hardly go bad another source is the door switches if they are grounding they will cause the module to operate continuosly.<P>------------------<BR>Keith<BR>85 SE Fiero 4.9L Caddy <BR>345hp||||reg||14
